  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing - staging-write `Permission denied`, not storage-full / DB-down / app-down.\n\n**What is happening:**\n\n* App `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` `Up 4 seconds` (E1), `running: true, exit_code: 0, oom_killed: false, restart_count: 0` running as `1000:1000` (E5).\n* `GET /health` returns `200` `{\"status\":\"ok\"}` (E2). App logs also show `GET /health ... 200 OK` after the failure (E12).\n* DB `incidentlab-db-1` is `running` `Up 10 seconds (healthy)` (E1), `health: healthy` (E10), postgres logs `database system is ready to accept connections` (E8), with `health_status: healthy` events (E7). No DB error in app traceback.\n* Bind is `/srv/lab-data` host -> `/data` container `rw: true` (E5).\n* Filesystem not full:\n  * `/srv/lab-data`: `use_percent: 9.0`, `available_mb: 410.7`, `inode_use_percent: 0.2` (E3).\n  * `/`: `use_percent: 6.8`, `available_mb: 91425.9`, `inode_use_percent: 1.5` (E11).\n* Upload path itself is writable:\n  * `/srv/lab-data/uploads`: `owner 1000:1000`, `mode 0755`, `app_user_can_write: true` (E6).\n  * `/srv/lab-data`: `owner 1000:1000`, `mode 0755`, `app_user_can_write: true` (E9).\n* Uploads worked then broke:\n  * `POST /upload ... 200 OK` twice at `23:36:24.69` and `23:36:24.76` (E12), with subsequent `GET /files/... 200 OK` and `DELETE ... 200 OK` (E12).\n  * Then `POST /upload ... 500 Internal Server Error` at `23:36:25.04` (E12) with `Exception in ASGI application` `Traceback` (E12).\n\n**Root cause vs symptom:**\n\n* Symptom: `POST /upload` `500` (E12).\n* Root cause observed: `File \"/app/main.py\", line 55, in upload` `with open(tmp_path, \"wb\") as out:` -> `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/tmp/5b092213988370ae71ba2c37eec98c7c.part'` (E4)(E12).\n  * That is host path `/srv/lab-data/tmp` via the `/data` bind (E5), not `/srv/lab-data/uploads` itself which remains writable (E6).\n\nRuled out as cause: app crash/down (E1)(E5)(E2), DB down/unhealthy (E1)(E10)(E8), disk / inode full on data filesystem (E3) or root filesystem (E11).\n\nUnderlying reason the `tmp` sub-directory/file became unwritable was not directly observable with available checks - only `uploads` (E6) and parent `lab-data` (E9) permission checks were available - but the failure itself is a staging-write permission failure.\n",
